---
// The home page. The first screen follows the tracker pattern's section 1.3 (ruled by John
// 2026-10-16) in the Belt Equation's layout: the thing held comes before the question. Left,
// in order: the eyebrow, the count in the largest type on the site with its claim and the
// five-rung totals under it, the question as the page title, one paragraph, the last-checked
// strip, two buttons. Right: the figure, the trunk's picture. Redesigned 2026-10-16 after John
// asked for the first screen to land the answer to the reader's question before anything else.
// Every number comes from tree.json (scripts/export.py).
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import { tree, longDate } from '../lib/tree';

const c = tree.counts;
const stages = tree.stages;
const examplesOnly = c.upgrades > 0 && c.examples === c.upgrades;
const plural = c.first_human_or_beyond === 1;
// The last-checked strip (tracker pattern section 5; copied from The Belt Equation's
// index.astro, `scan-strip`, on 2026-10-16): the date of the latest reading written out, how
// many upgrades were read, and what moved, with the one mover linked when there is exactly one.
const checked = tree.last_checked;
const loneMover = checked && checked.movers.length === 1 ? checked.movers[0] : null;
const movedLine = !checked
  ? ''
  : checked.moved === 0
    ? 'none moved'
    : checked.moved === 1
      ? 'one moved'
      : `${checked.moved} moved`;
---

<Base>
  <section class="home-first">
    <div class="first-main">
      <p class="eyebrow">A public count, kept in the open</p>
      <p class="big-number">{c.first_human_or_beyond}<small>of {c.upgrades}</small></p>
      <p class="big-claim">
        {plural ? 'way' : 'ways'} of changing a human being on purpose {plural ? 'has' : 'have'} been tried in at least one living person.
      </p>
      <div class="stage-row" aria-label="How many upgrades sit at each stage">
        {stages.map((s) => (
          <div>
            <span class="stat">{c.by_stage[s.key]}</span>
            <span class="stat-label">{s.label.toLowerCase()}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <h1 class="question">How much of a human being can we change on purpose today?</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Not in a story, and not someday: today, with a device, a drug or a procedure that at least one
        person has actually had, counted from the public record and never guessed. The one change that
        would matter most, a direct link between a brain and a machine, has a branch of its own.
      </p>
      <p class="scan-strip">
        <span class="strip-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>
          {checked
            ? <>Last checked {longDate(checked.date)}: {checked.upgrades_read} upgrade{checked.upgrades_read === 1 ? '' : 's'} read, {movedLine}{loneMover ? <>: <a href={loneMover.path}>{loneMover.name}</a></> : ''}{checked.flagged_waiting > 0 ? <>, {checked.flagged_waiting === 1 ? 'one thing' : `${checked.flagged_waiting} things`} waiting on me</> : ''}.
              {' '}<a href="/reading/">See the week's reading.</a>
              {checked.test && <span class="strip-test">This one is a hand-made test record; no real reading has run yet.</span>}</>
            : <>No reading of the news against the upgrades has run yet; the first one is coming, and this line will say when it ran.
              {' '}<a href="/reading/">About the weekly reading.</a></>}
        </span>
      </p>
      <p class="actions">
        <a class="btn" href="/branches/">What has been tried?</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/method/">Who is counting</a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="first-side figure-card">
      <p class="plate-label">Plate I · The seven branches</p>
      <Figure />
      <ul class="legend">
        <li><i class="stage-none"></i> nothing recorded yet</li>
        {stages.map((s) => <li><i class={`stage-${s.rank}`}></i> {s.label.toLowerCase()}</li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="figure-note">Each part of the figure is one of the seven branches, shaded by the furthest stage any upgrade under it has reached. Click a part to see what is there.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section explain narrow">
    <p>
      An <em>upgrade</em>, here, is one specific way of changing a human being on purpose: an implant that
      gives back some sight, a pill meant to slow ageing, a chip that lets a paralysed person type by
      thought. Each one is written down with a plain test of what would count as a person having it,
      the public record that settles that, and a <em>stage</em>: idea only, shown in animals, a first
      human, in use by doctors, or in wide use. The stage is a fact about what has happened, not a
      guess about what will. There are no odds on this site. The seven <em>branches</em> are the seven
      things about a person that can be changed: what they sense, how they move, how they think and
      remember, how they feel, how long they last, what they pass to their children, and how directly
      they can be joined to a machine.
    </p>
    {examplesOnly && (
      <p class="dim" style="font-size: 15px;">
        The {c.upgrades} upgrades on the tree today are examples, seeded on 16 October 2026 to show how the
        record works while the real list is written. Each says so on its page. The counts above will change
        as the list fills in.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shead"><h2>The seven branches</h2><span>what is recorded under each</span></div>
    <ul class="branches">
      {tree.branches.map((b) => (
        <li>
          <a class="bcard" href={b.path}>
            <div class="bcard-top"><span class="n">{b.order} of 7</span><span>{b.count === 0 ? 'nothing yet' : `${b.count} upgrade${b.count === 1 ? '' : 's'}`}</span></div>
            <div class="bcard-title">{b.name}</div>
            <div class="bcard-sub">{b.tagline}</div>
            <div class="bcard-foot">{b.furthest_label ? `Furthest stage: ${b.furthest_label.toLowerCase()}` : 'No stage reached'}</div>
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section narrow prose">
    <h2>Why keep count</h2>
    <p>
      One idea about the future says that as machines get smarter, people keep up by joining with
      them: better senses, better memory, a direct line from brain to computer. Whether that is
      happening is a question with an answer, and the answer is a list. This site is that list,
      kept in the open so that anyone can check an entry, argue with a stage, or add what is missing.
      The rules for deciding a stage are under <a href="/method/">how the numbers are worked out</a>,
      every change is dated in <a href="/story/">the story so far</a>, and <a href="/disagree/">here is how to tell me</a> if something is wrong.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
